  "usageDecisions": [
    "Client approval is explicitly staff-recorded. These labels assert no authenticated client action, signature, delivery or universal approval.",
    "Current and historical describe each decision's exact version and review epoch. They do not declare project completion or grant authority.",
    "Render the staff rich tag as bidi-isolated escaped text. The staffName parameter is an authorized display label, never a raw identity ID.",
    "Use clientApprovalRecordedUnknown when the recorder label is unavailable. Do not interpolate the unavailable message as a person's name or infer deletion or inactivity.",
    "Keep internal review time, reported client approval time and native recording time distinct. The visible display time zone comes from the chosen formatting preference, not an inferred client or business zone.",
    "Render version, evidence, contact and identity labels as plain bidi-isolated text. Copy supplies no link, preview fetch, permission, workflow or financial behavior."
  ],
